    {
      "text": "Instead of blood, a powerful magnetic force courses throughout Beldum’s body. This Pokémon communicates with others by sending controlled pulses of magnetism.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Beldum keeps itself floating by generating a magnetic force that repels earth’s natural magnetism. When it sleeps, this Pokémon anchors itself to a cliff using the hooks on its rear.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its cells are all magnets. It uses magnetism to communicate with others of its kind.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "With magnetic traction, it pulls its opponents in close. When they’re in range, it slashes them with its rear claws.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "Instead of blood, magnetism flows through its body. When it’s feeling bad, try giving it a magnet.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "If you anger it, it will do more than rampage. It will also burst out strong magnetism, causing nearby machines to break.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "From its rear, Beldum emits a magnetic force that rapidly pulls opponents in. They get skewered on Beldum’s sharp claws.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "The cells in this Pokémon’s body are composed of magnetic material. Instead of blood, magnetic forces flow through Beldum’s body.",
      "version": "shield"
    }
